{"page":"SCP2","gene":"SCP2","accession":"P22307","protein":"Sterol carrier protein 2","length":547,"disease":true,"events":["Alternative promoter usage","Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"P22307-1","name":"SCPx","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Plays a crucial role in the peroxisomal oxidation of branched-chain fatty acids (PubMed:10706581). Catalyzes the last step of the peroxisomal beta-oxidation of branched chain fatty acids and the side chain of the bile acid intermediates di- and trihydroxycoprostanic acids (DHCA and THCA) (PubMed:10706581). Also active with medium and long straight chain 3-oxoacyl-CoAs. Stimulates the microsomal conversion of 7-dehydrocholesterol to cholesterol and transfers phosphatidylcholine and 7-dehydrocholesterol between membrances, in vitro (By similarity). Isoforms SCP2 and SCPx cooperate in peroxisomal oxidation of certain naturally occurring tetramethyl-branched fatty acyl-CoAs (By similarity)"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000371514.8"],"refseq":["NM_002979.5"],"refseqProteins":["NP_002970.2"],"maneSelect":true},"model":{"entry":"AF-P22307-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P22307-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":92.3,"plddt":[[0,2],[50,7],[70,2],[90,17],[70,4],[90,94],[70,6],[90,276],[70,4],[50,3],[0,11],[50,3],[70,3],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,3],[90,1],[70,7],[90,2],[70,1],[90,1],[70,2],[90,11],[70,5],[90,9],[70,1],[90,1],[70,1],[90,4],[70,6],[90,12],[70,15],[90,8],[70,12],[50,2],[0,6]]}},"features":[{"type":"Modified residue","start":3,"end":3,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Site","start":20,"end":21,"description":"Cleavage"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":132,"end":132,"description":"N6-acetyllysine; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":132,"end":132,"description":"N6-succinyllysine; alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":168,"end":168,"description":"N6-succinyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":173,"end":173,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"